            <h3 id="player">Unlimited <em>Player</em> license</h3>
            <p>
                Do you need to run your macros on many machines and/or servers? Or do you need to distribute the solutions you create to many users
                within (or even outside) your organization? Then you can purchase the <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> Enterprise Player license. It gives you an
                <span class="hiblue">unlimited license</span> to run your macros and testsuites on as many machines as you need
                - inside or outside your company or organization. This license can be purchased separately at any time, or you purchase it as part of the <em>*Special Player Bundle*</em> (see the <a href="#volume">price list above</a>).


            <p>
                The <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> Enterprise Player has <span class="hiblue"><em>all features of Enterprise Edition</em>,  except the ability to create new macros</span>. Technically speaking if <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> XModules are unlocked with the Player license key,
                the "Save" button is disabled. Everything else works 100% as in the regular Enterprise Edition.  The number of included OCR conversions is 10,000 <em>per day</em> per Player license (additional conversions can be purchased any time).
            </p>

            <p>
                Last but not least note that other RPA vendors often call such a Player license "attended bots", " unattended bots" or "Orchestrator license". We at Ui.Vision
                do <em>not</em> distinguish between attended
                or unattended bots, and we do <em>not</em> charge you per bot. The Enterprise Player license gives you an unlimited number of attended and unattended bots.

            </p>

            <h3 id="faq">Purchasing RPA - FAQ</h3>

            <h4 id="q1">Q1: On how many browsers can I use the license key?</h4>
            <p>
                <small>
                    Q1: On how many browsers can I use the license key? As a developer I use on the same computer Chrome and Edge next to each other. Can I use my license key on only one or the other browser type?
                </small>
            </p>
            <p>
                A1: The licensing is per seat/PC/Mac. So you can use a license key on all browser types (Chrome, Firefox, Edge) <em>and</em> on each with unlimited browser profiles and it still counts only
                as one license.
            </p>

            <h4 id="q2">Q2: How often can I (re-)enter a license key?</h4>
            <p>
                A2: You can uninstall/reinstall and re-enter your license keys unlimited times. This can be done on the same <em>or other machines</em>. The only limit is that not more than
                "X" installations of Ui.Vision RPA PRO are active (running!) at the same time. "X" is the number of licenses you purchased.
            </p>

            <h4 id="q3">Q3: What happens after a year of free PRO upgrades? Do I have to renew?</h4>
            <p>
                <small>
                    Q3: On the top of this page it says, the license key will only cover updates on the RPA  software for a year. Usually the RPA extension updates automatically
                    without me able to prevent doing so. So what happens if RPA updates more than a year later?
                    Do I have to buy a new license key to keep having access to the extended functionality?
                </small>
            </p>
            <p>
                While the official license information states that "only" one year of free upgrades are included we have provided free upgrades since the start - which is meanwhile
                more than five years ago. We have no plans to change this. So you can expect that you will receive free upgrades for the foreseeable future. We do not want to promise free upgrades "forever" since, well, our ability to look into the
                future is just as limited as yours. But we can sure you that if we ever start charging for upgrades it will only be for new - yet to be added - features.
                <em>Our guarantee is that all currently existing features will continue to work without any further payments.</em>
            </p>
            <p>
                The "only" thing that will stop is the included free PRO/Enterprice level priority support. To continue getting priority support we recommend to renew your license for 25% of the license fee. However, if you choose not to do this, your software continues to work and no features are disabled.
            </p>
            <h4 id="q4">Q4: How to move a license to a new machine?</h4>
            <p>
                <small>
                    Q4: We are moving our virtual machines to a different setup and I would like
                    to know how we can transfer our RPA license for the same users to the new machine?
                </small>
            </p>
            <p>
                A4: Please see answer #2 above. Simply stop using RPA on the old machines and re-enter the license key on the new machines.
                You do <em>not</em> have to uninstall RPA on the old machines. Just no longer using it is sufficient.

            </p>




